1. Partial handbook text only. The OHOTMU volumes on archive.org are lending-library scans. I could read only the full-text search snippets (about 100 OCR characters each), and the search-inside page (inside.php) returned 403. So:
   - issue numbers and pages are unconfirmed (for example, the Asgardians group entry is probably Deluxe #1);
   - some sentences are joined from overlapping snippets, and their opening words are missing in places (Colossus's "The means by which").

2. Entries I could not see at all:
   - the OHOTMU Thing, Wolverine, Luke Cage and individual Thor entries;
   - OHOTMU: Daredevil 2004 (the source of the fan-wiki Kingpin "9 pounds of fat");
   - OHOTMU Master Edition #9 (the fan-wiki Black Panther "denser tissue");
   - Thor & Hercules: Encyclopaedia Mythologica 2009;
   - the OHOTMU A to Z (2008-10) volumes for these characters.

3. Numbers no source gives:
   - Wolverine's adamantium mass appears only on Marvel.com (105 lb / 47.6 kg); no handbook figure turned up, and "nearly 100 pounds" is fan-wiki text;
   - no source states a tissue density in kg/m3, the Thing's hide mass, the mass of Juggernaut's helmet or armour, or the mass of Doomsday's bone spurs.

4. DC sources: DC's own Who's Who (1985-87, 1990-92) was not found. DC coverage rests on two DK books plus fan wikis.

5. Marvel.com access: WebFetch returned 403 for Marvel.com. The pages were fetched with curl and a browser user agent on 2026-10-11 (raw copies in scratchpad/research/comic-composition/raw/).

6. Not used as sources: archive.org also holds unauthorised digital comic uploads (for example the Marvel Masterworks Thor digital upload and the "Kileko-Empire" collections) that repeat the handbook wording; I deliberately did not cite them.

7. Unresolved Thor ambiguity: OHOTMU says "flesh and bone" (whole body) and DK says "skin and bones". If only skin and bone are denser, the correction is smaller. That case was not computed, because it needs tissue mass fractions that were outside this topic.

